    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I've got a heifer that just came out of rumenotomy about 6 hours ago. I need a clear protocol for what I should be looking out for over the next few days regarding the incision site and any internal signs of trouble or infection. Also, what's the plan for getting her back on feed?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For the next few days, watch your heifer's incision site for signs of infection, like excessive swelling, redness, discharge that smells foul, or heat around the wound. Keep an eye out for signs of internal distress, such as lethargy, refusal to stand, fever, or abdominal pain. If she seems to be doing well, you can start offering small amounts of feed, gradually increasing the amount as she shows improvement. If you notice any concerning signs, contact your veterinarian immediately.",
      "source": "target",
